<title>PAKISTAN: U.S. agency to give $10 mln aid to Pakistan.</title>
<headline>U.S. agency to give $10 mln aid to Pakistan.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Commodity Credit Corporation will give $10 million to help Pakistan develop its oilseed industry under an agreement signed in Islamabad on Tuesday, a Pakistan government statement said.</p>
<p>It said the agreement was signed under the U.S.  PL-480 (food-for-peace) Programme.</p>
</text>
